@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.6.0
@changelog
  - Codename: Six Seasons and a Movie
  - Soft-key sets: nine of them, each with a number and a name. Soft-Key Set, engage takes the set number as its parameter, so a set sits on any key, a foot switch or a Stream Deck tile. Sets 8 and 9 are the two Layer 1 coordinates that carry SSL's own channel-strip and bus-comp rows, editable now wherever the plug-in leaves a key free, and added as 8 and 9 rather than renumbering 1 to 7, because bindings point at these numbers.
  - The matrix is the editor: nine rows, six columns. Click a cell to go to that bank on the surface and in the editor, double-click to rename it, right-click for copy, cut and paste of the whole bank, its dynamic kind, your presets and the factory banks.
  - A bank can be named, and the name is announced in the mode-change banner and listed in the focused-track panel. The set comes first, so a bank called KHE Amps in a set called User 1 reads User 1, KHE Amps.
  - New: OBS on the keys, over obs-websocket. Start and stop recording with a lamp that follows what OBS reports rather than what the key asked for, pause, chapter marks, and scene switching. A soft-key bank of kind OBS Scenes shows the scene names live with the one on air lit, and a marker named "obs: Wide" switches as the playhead passes it.
  - OBS scenes can be bound by name instead of by position, so reordering the scene list in OBS no longer repoints the keys silently. The old number still works.
  - Sticky Pot: a pin can carry a second parameter on the same pot, counter-running by default, which is how an 1176 is driven harder without the level moving. Both values are anchored when you pair them so nothing jumps, and moving either by hand afterwards is picked up from there. A pane of its own lists every pin in the project.
  - Fixed: letting go of the fader under FLIP wrote the focused parameter, or pan, instead of the pinned one. The release path was meant to mirror the live one and had every rung but that one.
  - Fixed: UF8 in a Send or Receive fader mode showed the level and the comp and gate GR of the track that would sit on the strip without the mode, while the name was the send's. All three now follow the send's destination or the receive's source, and a hardware output or an empty slot stays dark. The channel number follows it too. SEL and fader-touch select do nothing on a send strip and its lamp is dark, since selecting would change the track and empty the faders; Solo and Cut act on the send as before. The same for the UF1 as the Extender's ninth send strip, which also takes the send's colour now, like the UF8.
  - The Learn HUD's parameter list says where each parameter already sits: the slot on the UC1, the bank and strip on the UF8, the EXT FUNCS cells. Those cells are visible and assignable there too, with rename and clear.
  - AutoLearn moved into the HUD's parameter drawer: it proposes for the plug-in the HUD is showing, for the tab you are on, recognises a channel matrix, maps a plug-in that has no map, numbers EQ bands by their number, no longer matches Knee to Mix, refuses to write into a factory map, lists what it did not match, and stays on the plug-in you just mapped.
  - UF1: both footswitches are bindable, the preset browser owns its screen and reads SSL's own on-disk library for an SSL plug-in and REAPER's for everything else, opening on Shift + 5-8 in the Plugin view, four keys carry a binding per view, and Fades mode can show REAPER's crossfade editor while the edge you aim at is a crossfade.
  - Speed: the push-cycle menus and the FX-Learn parameter lists were rebuilding on every tick and every frame, which a plug-in with hundreds of parameters turned into a two-second wait after each click. Built once now, indexed rather than scanned, and written when the edits stop.
  - Windows: the combined FX-Learn layer is left Alt with left Ctrl.
  - Metering: gain reduction reads per strip on all eight UF8 strips, seven of which had been dark since April. Gate GR is there too, including the 32Classic's, and Combine GR composes with the source instead of being gated by it.
  - Fixed: FX Learn follows the plug-in the Learn HUD is on, and nothing else. Switching a map to "UF1 only" fills the UF1 layer first, a learned channel strip puts its soft-keys where a factory one has them, Create plus AutoLearn goes straight to the proposals, the listening run stops only at slots that have a UC1 control, UF1 pages turn by hand outside PLUGIN mode, and EXT FUNCS are learned by clicking the slot and wiggling the control.
  - New: a press on a surface selects that button in Settings, Bindings. Switchable under Behaviour, Bindings; the key that opens and closes Settings keeps working.
  - Fixed: with "Layers switch Quicks only" on, the Bindings pane shows the layer that fires instead of the layer that banks, so a binding no longer looks deleted while the key goes on firing it.
  - New: a long-press slot can repeat while the key is held. First shot at the half second as before, the rest at 20 to 1000 ms, 100 by default. Greyed out on an action that toggles.
  - New: REC steps a track's input channel without an RME interface. The input is REAPER's own; only preamp gain, 48V, pad and phase need TotalReaper.
  - Fixed: in REC + RME the value line belongs to the preamp on all three surfaces, and a hardware input without a preamp shows empty flags and "--dB" instead of pan on the UF1 or a stale reading on the UC1.
  - Fixed: a fresh REAPER never starts in UF8 Plug-in Mode, and a press the mode swallows flashes the banner.
  - Fixed: the banking window counts the strips that show a track, so DynaMount stands and Hue lamps no longer hide the tracks behind them.
  - Fixed: a failed surface reopen is retried every five seconds instead of once, so a UC1 that drops out comes back by itself.
  - Fixed: all three surfaces name the hardware input the REC keys are driving. The UC1 only flashed it for a second and a half after a channel change and then went back to naming the plug-in; it stands in the colour bar and in the model field now, from the same source as the UF8 and the UF1, and it repaints when the input changes.
  - Fixed: pointing a track from a channel with a preamp at one without left the old gain on the UC1, the one surface that does not rebuild its value line every tick.
  - Fixed: UF1 V-Pot push and UF1 Sends/Receives toggle could not be picked in Bindings. Both were bindable and sat in no category, and the picker drops a builtin whose category is empty, so the only way onto a key was to already have it on one. Hardware Modes and Sends / Receives now, and the check CI runs fails on any builtin the picker cannot show.
  - Nav Mode was rebuilt around the question it answers: one row per question, one column per surface, each surface with its own display switch and its own actions. The UF1 is in it, Nav lands on its soft-keys and its channel encoder, Regions and Markers are two lists of their own, Bank pages the marker list, and the time field says where a jump went. Markers in region is a setting now.
  - New: Sleep, under Settings, Devices, Brightness. The surfaces go to zero brightness after 1 to 99 minutes idle, SSL 360's own range, off by default. Playing or recording counts as activity, any key, fader or knob wakes them, and that first touch only wakes. Sleep now is a built-in action for a key.
  - Helper text became hover boxes under Devices, Appearance, Behaviour and 26 more panes, so the panes are shorter and the explanation sits at the control.
  - The GR calibration is captured, not typed: drive the compressor to a point you can see, press capture, and the scale follows from that one point. The UF1's comp GR reads through the same calibration.
  - Fixed: the analogue needle and the overload LEDs run on the real stream again. A meter frame that leaves the data type out means VuPpm, and the parser threw exactly those frames away; the needle had been emulated against that gap.
  - Fixed: the goniometer draws at full width. Its payload is 17113 four-bit cells, not 8557 bytes, so half the horizontal resolution was being thrown away, and the brightness ramp added on top was fighting the aliasing it caused.
  - Fixed: a setting that returns to zero arrives. In SSL's protocol a field at its default is left out, so a value of exactly 0 looked like an absent field and the old one stood.
  - Fixed: four ways to lose REAPER or the picture, all closed: a plug-in bypassed, taken offline or stepped through presets from the USB thread, an empty Focus Set pin with the Extender on, a paint on the UF1, and a project load that left the surface blank.
  - Text widths are the ones the displays have: eight characters on the UF8, eight on the UF1, twelve on the UC1. Names had been abbreviated to widths that never existed, and a long parameter name bled into the UF8's yellow value zone.
  - The MCP inserts overlay keeps up with the chain: adding a plug-in no longer leaves it short, a move into an empty slot redraws, the frame follows an FX that slides into a free slot, and it redraws when the highlighted row moves.
  - Favourites housekeeping: a clean-up button for favourites whose plug-in lost its mapping, un-learning no longer leaves a favourite that clones itself, switching a favourite moves the FX-Learn editor and the Learn HUD with it, and the carousel reads the short name.
  - The UF1 joined the brightness sliders and has a column of its own for its displays; 0x47 turned out to be a panel master, and the LCD slider had been dimming the LEDs with it.
  - Fixed: banners tell the truth about who caused them. The first mode change of a run used to be swallowed as a baseline, and the Extender's own announcement could eat the one your keypress had earned.
  - The plug-in says what it is, and what it is sending. The handshake carries the type, so a Meter, a Meter Pro and a channel strip are told apart instead of guessed at, and the prepare messages are read: the readouts wear the names the plug-in gives them, and a mono meter gets the mono faceplate instead of the stereo one. Only real data frames are parsed as meters.
  - HQ Mode and A/B go over the protocol where the plug-in offers it and fall back to the chunk where it does not. The EQ graph's last point is the curve rather than a fixed 0 dB, so the step at the 20 kHz edge is gone, and the meter ring's AUTO position says AUTO.
  - Still open from the twelve findings behind this metering round: the plug-in selection LED, which needs an instance identity that does not depend on the instance streaming first, and the multi-channel overview, which needs a surround Meter Pro to test against.
  - The jog wheel has modes, and each one edits something. In Items the wheel walks the item selection and the nav cross extends it along the edge it is travelling toward, with your own position taken up again when the axis changes, and item grouping is honoured by REAPER rather than worked out here.
  - Each surface is fully usable without the others. Fourteen places had a feature standing on a device that was not plugged in: the Extender layout, the Nav overlay, the pinned startup bank, the Learn-HUD's UF8 tab, the colour bar naming a cycled plug-in, the UF8's gain-reduction rows. All of them stand on their own now.
  - EXT FUNCS read SSL's own list: for each factory strip the entries come from what the plug-in puts on the wire, in SSL's order, rather than from a rule of ours. "Whatever is not already on a knob" is wrong, seven entries of the 32C list sit on its V-Pots at the same time.
  - A learned channel strip lands where a factory one does: its soft-keys take the factory positions on the UF1 instead of filling from the top, and the Bus Comp gets the factory UF1 layout as well. The EQ graph no longer draws a strip's curve under a plug-in that has no EQ.
  - A factory bank longer than eight keys spills into Shift. Encoder Modes carries all fifteen encoder modes that way, eight on Plain and seven on Shift, one modifier apart, and saving a bank of your own as a preset takes its Shift half with it.
  - UF8 Plug-in Mode ships on Shift + PLUGIN, and Esc really cancels an armed learn.
  - The number above the UF1 fader names what the fader moves, in the unit the plug-in gave it, and a frequency reads the same on every surface.
  - Parameter Groups wear a colour, one per group, on the bank's keys.
  - Modifier modes and automation keys: the UF1's Solo and Cut honour the keyboard modifier modes, the Extender knows all four route modes, and the automation-mode keys set every selected track.
  - One more colour: palette index 0x0C renders on the hardware and had been thrown away for five months, so track colours quantise onto twelve entries instead of eleven. An LED override on a key's plain slot could be in force and unreachable at the same time; it is reachable.
  - The focused-track panel got proper rows, and centring that centres.
  - The Harrison 32Classic Channel Strip v2 is a factory strip, on the UF8, the UC1 and the UF1, with its gate gain reduction, its own presets in the preset browser, its A/B, its PRE key and its EXT FUNCS list as SSL sends it. The 4K strips got their soft-key pages as SSL 360 2.1.12 lays them out, including the colour-dependent LF/HF key on the 4K G and a tenth UF1 page, EXPANDER.
  - The UF1's soft-key banks got the UF8's editor: ten banks in a matrix, the cell is the editor, rename in the header with the panel showing the name as it is typed, right-click for copy, cut, paste and clear, bank presets and a pinned startup bank. Encoder and Jog mode are drop-downs, and uf1_bank_select reaches the UF8 as well.
  - SSL 360 2.1.12 changed what SSL's own software draws on the UF1, and the meter view was measured against it again: the VU needle falls the way SSL draws it, through the plug-in's half-second hold, instead of dropping between messages; the overload LED holds its flash for 100 ms instead of blinking once per paint; the goniometer trail fades like light and takes the brightest cell per pixel; the time field keeps running in the meter view; and the encoder and jog pickers list what SSL lists.
  - The UF8 encoder modes are REAPER actions, fifteen of them, one per mode, so a mode reaches a keyboard shortcut, a foot switch or a Stream Deck tile. The encoder no longer swallows the first click after a direction reversal.
  - Seven printed keys that did nothing now do what they say: NORM, REC, AUTO, NAV, NUDGE, FOCUS and the channel-encoder push ship bound. An existing configuration is left as it is.
  - A soft-key slot draws its whole step chain: add a step, set its type and its wait, and a Note On, a pause and a Note Off sit on one press. The dispatch has run chains for months, the editor showed only the first step.
  - CS and BC favourites are dynamic bank kinds, which retired the two factory banks that did the same by hand and gave back two of the six places in a set.
  - Two more dynamic bank kinds, and the manual's table lists all eight: the eight Hue scene slots, reachable before but undocumented, and the OBS scenes.
  - Every built-in action brings a twelve-character default label, in the Label field the moment you pick the action, until you type one of your own. A build without a label or a description for a new action fails, so the gap cannot reach a release.
  - FLIP and Strip Mode couple both ways, and FLIP with PAN reaches the fader in Strip Mode. FLIP never puts a binary parameter on the fader, the fader stops commandeering the V-Pots, and under FLIP the UF1's two rows show two different things. A fader reaches 100 % of a parameter rather than 99.9, touching one no longer changes the channel, and a move no longer takes the focused parameter with it.
  - Pan in SSL Strip Mode belongs to the strip: the V-Pot shows the pan it writes, Force Pan drives the strip's own pan, the UF1's pan knob sits on the strip's pan with or without the Extender, and panning no longer takes the focused parameter.
  - Touch to Learn puts the UF8 into Plug-in Mode by itself, because mapping a plug-in while the surface shows the project is not possible. A fader arms its cell while the mode is armed instead of driving its parameter, and the PLUG-IN key is the way back out.
  - One answer to the question "which plug-in is in play": the UF8, the UF1 and the panels asked it in their own ways and could disagree. There is one resolver now, the UF1 reads it, and an open plug-in window outranks a surface FX you cannot see.
  - Panel LEDs say what the key does: a key cleared to Do nothing no longer sits bright in its active colour, the PLUGIN lamp follows its binding, and the Auto row reads the layer the surface fires.
  - More from the day at the desk: a plug-in already mapped on the UC1 and the UF1 can be learned on the UF8 too, the UF8 fader learn no longer depends on an open plug-in window, no fader is pre-ticked anywhere, AutoLearn stops proposing the same parameter twice and says what it did, it stops asking again for the mode you just picked, and "don't show offline FX" applies to every answer instead of only the last one.
  - On TotalReaper's side, the preamp keys work with its routing mirror switched off. The mirror had gated every write to TotalMix, so a gain moved on the surface, landed in the track's ExtState and never reached the interface, while the readback it was compared against came in regardless. Writing follows reading now, for the preamps and for Dim, Mono, Speaker B, Talkback and the snapshot slots. Needs TotalReaper 0.2.4.
  - Smaller, still visible: ReaEQ's band width converts between octaves and Q, the parameter pickers hide REAPER's MIDI-learn entries, the bindings page and the Learn HUD agree on what learning and unbinding mean, a renamed parameter reads the same on all three panels, a UF8 relearn resets invert, an Exchange map can no longer be shadowed by the one it replaces, and Hue labels take eight characters.
  - The bindings file moves to version 42. Every step is additive and a v0.5.9 setup loads unchanged.
